<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 48 0 R
/T (If the district total were accumulated in double instead of long long, it would not normally overflow at this scale, but it could introduce rounding error because decimal currency values are not always represented exactly in binary. Each addition is O\(1\), and the total operation over n bills is O\(n\) for either type. Storage per accumulator is O\(1\). The primary reason to choose long long paise is exactness, not speed.)
/E (If the district total were accumulated in double instead of long long, it would not normally overflow at this scale, but it could introduce rounding error because decimal currency values are not always represented exactly in binary. Each addition is O\(1\), and the total operation over n bills is O\(n\) for either type. Storage per accumulator is O\(1\). The primary reason to choose long long paise is exactness, not speed.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
