/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (The program meets the main single-household requirements by computing progressive slabs, adding the fixed charge, rejecting invalid input and handling the specified meter rollover. Integer paise avoids ordinary currency rounding errors, while long long supports large accumulated totals more safely than int. For smart meters, the best direction is a modified billing engine with interval readings, peak-time pricing, validated external tariff configuration and scalable storage. Before submission, compile and run the code on your own lab computer, attach actual output screenshots, and add the GitHub repository link requested by the lab.)
/E (The program meets the main single-household requirements by computing progressive slabs, adding the fixed charge, rejecting invalid input and handling the specified meter rollover. Integer paise avoids ordinary currency rounding errors, while long long supports large accumulated totals more safely than int. For smart meters, the best direction is a modified billing engine with interval readings, peak-time pricing, validated external tariff configuration and scalable storage. Before submission, compile and run the code on your own lab computer, attach actual output screenshots, and add the GitHub repository link requested by the lab.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
