<<
/Title (Float-versus-integer comparison: a float or double can represent many decimal values only approximately. Summing a large number of bill amounts can accumulate small rounding differences. Integer paise is exact for two-decimal currency, provided overflow is prevented. A double accumulator is easy to use but requires rounding rules and is not preferred for financial totals.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 632 0 R
/Prev 653 0 R
>>
endobj
