644 0 obj
<<
/Title (Limitations: the sample program processes one household at a time, assumes the specified 16-bit meter range and exact rollover condition, and does not store customer records or write bills to a database. District-scale use needs persistent storage, duplicate-reading checks, audit logs, access controls, backup, and explicit handling for meter replacements and multiple rollovers.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 624 0 R
/Prev 634 0 R
/Next 645 0 R
>>
endobj
645 0 obj
<<
/Title (Tariff revision approach: store validated rates and slab limits in a configuration file or database table, load them when the program starts, and record a version/effective date for each tariff. Validate that limits increase and rates are non-negative. This avoids recompilation for every tariff change, but it adds file I/O, parsing, validation and a risk of a missing or malformed configuration file.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 624 0 R
/Prev 644 0 R
/Next 635 0 R
>>
endobj
