<<
/Title (C type discussion: the C standard guarantees minimum ranges, not that int is always 32 bits or long is always 64 bits. On many 64-bit Windows compilers, long is still 32 bits; on common 64-bit Linux systems, long is 64 bits. long long is at least 64 bits. Use limits from limits.h and check multiplication/addition bounds if a production system accepts unbounded input.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 632 0 R
/Prev 660 0 R
/Next 641 0 R
>>
